    "notes": {
        "63c7feab-f770-478e-8325-350b70a77655": {
            "x": 64,
            "y": 432,
            "width": 736,
            "height": 288,
            "content": "## Test data assumption: one real Nuki device\n\nNuki has no sandbox. The connected account (API token with the scopes smartlock.readOnly, smartlock.action, smartlock.auth and smartlock.log) must hold at least one Smart Lock that is online. The flow takes the first device Find Smartlocks returns, so no device ID is hardcoded.\n\n**The flow physically locks the device.** Run it only on a test lock, not on a door somebody depends on.\n\nThe trigger polls and records the existing log on its first check, so the lock command is sent after a 2-minute Wait. Do not remove it. The trigger watches all devices of the account for \"Lock\" entries; another person locking a device during the run also satisfies it."
        }
    }
